body:
I've tried implementing a solution that just offsets the underline columns by the difference between `old_column` and `new_column`. So far it seems to be working well enough:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e071b89d-de02-4f92-8b46-ce1eab9bb61b

```cpp
int col_delta = new_column - old_column;
for (Underline &u : underlines) {
	if (u.start_line == new_line) {
		u.start_column += col_delta;
	}

	if (u.end_line == new_line) {
		u.end_column += col_delta;
	}
}
```
I have a slight suspicion there might be some edge case not occurring to me right now, since this is relatively so simple 😅 But again, IMO since Godot re-evaluates the underlines immediately anyways, a moment or two of underlines being a bit off doesn't feel like a terrible thing. So, I think it likely makes sense to go with this for now.

