body:
GDScript doesn't use ScriptLanguageExtension right? We should be able to keep the more detailed info for errors for GDScript but not use it in `ScriptLanguageExtension::validate`.

Basically, revert back to [2407ecd](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/2407ecdefd19968c3cdb8c40948715f0ba504167) and in `ScriptLanguageExtension::validate` do
```cpp
serr.start_line = err["line"];
serr.end_line = err["line"];
serr.start_column = err["column"];
serr.end_column = err["column"];
```
instead of using `err.has("start_line")` etc.

